&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UX strategy and quality across four core areas of Operations: menu planning and food systems (algorithmic menu planning, ranking, demand forecasting, assortment), fulfillment (production, order management, inventory, logistics, manufacturing, supplier reliability), an internal operations-research platform that runs dozens of optimization models across the supply chain, and the technology backbone that keeps our warehouses and production sites running.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continued build-out of an AI-native design practice: extending our design system directly into AI-assisted workflows, and using that as proof that UX can lead — not just support — the company&#39;s AI-first agenda.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Service design for the internal-facing tools that operators, planners and analysts depend on every day — often the least glamorous and highest-impact surface area in the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Talent leadership for a distributed team spanning multiple geographies: hiring, career development, and consistent design-quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A seat at the Operations leadership table, partnering directly with the senior Product and Engineering leaders for the organization, and representing UX&#39;s interests in company-wide strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
