&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.2;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: tahoma, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;ClinChoice is a global full-service CRO committed to professional growth and a quality-driven “one-team” culture. We are seeking a Senior/ Principal Statistician to join our in-house team and support projects across a diverse client portfolio, including pharmaceutical, biotechnology, medical device, and consumer health companies of varying sizes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.2;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: tahoma, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;We are seeking an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Senior/Principal Statistician&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Consultant &lt;/strong&gt;to provide statistical leadership and expertise across clinical development programs within the pharmaceutical industry. The successful candidate will contribute to clinical trial design, statistical methodology, data analysis, and regulatory submissions while collaborating with cross-functional teams to support evidence generation and informed decision-making throughout drug development.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.2;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: tahoma, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: tahoma, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Provide statistical leadership across clinical development programs, from early-phase studies through late-phase clinical trials.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: tahoma, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Lead clinical trial design, including endpoint selection, sample size calculations, power analyses, and randomization strategies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: tahoma, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Develop and review clinical study protocols, statistical analysis plans (SAPs), and other statistical documentation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: tahoma, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Oversee statistical analyses and interpretation of clinical trial data to ensure scientific rigor and regulatory compliance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: tahoma, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Provide statistical expertise for regulatory submissions and interactions with health authorities, including the FDA and EMA.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: tahoma, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Collaborate with Clinical Development, Clinical Operations, Data Management, Regulatory Affairs, and Medical Writing teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Every day, tens of millions of people come to Roblox to explore, create, play, learn, and connect with friends in 3D immersive digital experiences– all created by our global community of developers and creators.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Roblox, we’re building the tools and platform that empower our community to bring any experience that they can imagine to life. Our vision is to reimagine the way people come together, from anywhere in the world, and on any device.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re on a mission to connect a billion people with optimism and civility, and looking for amazing talent to help us get there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A career at Roblox means you’ll be working to shape the future of human interaction, solving unique technical challenges at scale, and helping to create safer, more civil shared experiences for everyone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Director, Developer Relations – &lt;/strong&gt;Europe, you will lead Roblox’s developer ecosystem strategy and growth across Europe. You will be accountable for defining the regional strategy, establishing the partnerships and programs required to execute it, and delivering measurable outcomes for the Roblox developer ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build deep relationships with leading developers, studios, publishers, technology partners, and emerging creators while identifying the next generation of high-potential partners for Roblox. You will serve as a senior representative of Roblox within the regional games and technology industries and as an executive-level advocate for the needs and opportunities of developers within Roblox.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires both strategic vision and operational leadership. You will translate Roblox’s global priorities into a regional strategy, identify opportunities and barriers to ecosystem growth, and mobilize teams across Product, Engineering, Marketing, Partnerships, Creator, and International to deliver against those opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in developer relations, games, partnerships, platform strategy, or related fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced leading regional or ecosystem strategy with measurable business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply knowledgeable about the games and developer landscape in Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to influence senior internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven, strategic, and comfortable operating in ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with Roblox Studio, Unity, Unreal, or similar development tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&

&lt;h2&gt;About us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://constructorlabs.org/&quot;&gt;Constructor Labs&lt;/a&gt; is the research arm of Constructor Knowledge, based at Campus Ring 1 in Bremen, Germany. Our work is organized around three units: Knowledge Labs, Cyber Labs and Science Labs. We apply computing, software and robotics research to make scientists, teachers and students more effective, working with institutional partners that include CERN, NUS, Carnegie Mellon and Fraunhofer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our &lt;a href=&quot;https://constructorlabs.org/solutions/edtech/&quot;&gt;EdTech practice&lt;/a&gt; produces research that runs in production. AI-supported remote proctoring is in use at the Irish Aviation Authority, Princess Nourah University and Saudi Electronic University, and our course delivery platform is used by CERN, EPFL, MariaDB and Acronis. For industry clients, we build tailored BSc, MSc and PhD pipelines, L&amp;amp;D operating models, AI upskilling programmes and customer training systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Constructor Labs Solutions (CLS)&lt;/strong&gt; is our client-facing systems integrator for the education and research sector, launching in September 2026. It brings audit and consultancy, content, platform, talent and R&amp;amp;D services together under a single contract, an offer few providers make to education buyers today. Delivery is orchestrated across several Constructor organizations: CUB, Nexford, Nexademy, EBAC, Constructor Labs and Constructor Tech. Our aim is to become the go-to systems integrator for education in EMEA by 2029.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will open EMEA markets for Constructor Labs Solutions as a quota-carrying individual contributor. The role rests on an established network among universities, online education providers, EdTech vendors and corporate L&amp;amp;D and research buyers, and on your ability to convert that network into signed engagements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work with the marketing and delivery teams to build pipeline, establish the CLS brand and develop a case-study library. Supporting you are a credible research institution, named production references, an existing Constructor and Constructor Tech client base, and delivery capability across five service lines that can be combined into a single proposal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The sales motion is consultative. Engagements typically open with a low-risk paid diagnostic (Technology Landscape Assessment, Curriculum Gap Analysis or Learning Strategy Advisory), which you then convert into a multi-line implementation or managed-service mandate. Initial engagements start at around €150–250K in lifetime value and grow from there. Sales cycles in public higher education run six to twelve months, so you will manage a long-cycle institutional funnel alongside faster corporate L&amp;amp;D deals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Reporting and scope&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to:&lt;/str

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Remote within Europe, with regular presence in Bremen&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct Reports: &lt;/strong&gt;None initially; technical leadership across the engineering group&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Mission&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the architecture of the software platform on which Constructor Labs&#39; quantum group builds. The platform drives physical quantum hardware end to end — calibration, orchestration, experiment execution and device state — and must work both in our own cloud and on customer premises, including restricted and air-gapped environments. The Principal Architect sets the technical direction, makes the structural decisions, and is the senior engineering voice in a group where research and engineering sit closely together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 1 Platform Architecture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end architecture across backend services, job orchestration, hardware abstraction and device state management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the interfaces between the scientific layer and the platform layer so physicists can work without engineering support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make and carry the build-versus-buy and framework decisions; document them so they survive the people who made them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the migration of the platform onto the Constructor technology stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Success Metrics and KPIs: architectural decisions documented and adopted, platform stability, migration delivered to plan.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 2 Hands-on Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write production code in the core of the system, not only design documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the hardest components personally — those where correctness and performance both matter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and enforce engineering standards: testing, review, structured logging, dependency governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remove single points of failure so no component has only one person who understands it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Success Metrics and KPIs: test coverage, review discipline, bus factor above one on every core component.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 3 Working with Research&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work day to day with research physicists, translating experimental workflows into software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep the research and engineering collaboration model intact as the group grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the product function with realistic estimates and honest technical constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Accountability: research team able to run experiments without engineering bottlenecks.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;Remote within Europe, with regular presence in Bremen&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct Reports:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;None initially&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Model: &lt;/strong&gt;Remote / hybrid. Regular time on-site in Bremen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Mission&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the product direction for Constructor&#39;s quantum software line and act as the bridge between a research group and a technology platform. This is a hands-on role in a small technical team, not portfolio management. The Head of Product decides what gets built, keeps research and engineering pointed at something shippable, and owns the relationship with the customers and partners who use it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 1 Product Direction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the roadmap for the quantum software line and the decisions behind it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define which capabilities go into the Constructor technology platform and in what order.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate research capability into product that someone outside the group will pay for or use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kill work that is not going anywhere, and say so clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Success Metrics and KPIs: roadmap delivered, features adopted, decisions made and held.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 2 Research and Engineering Interface&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sit between physicists and engineers and keep both productive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run planning and prioritisation for a small, senior, opinionated team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold the technical depth to challenge both sides rather than relay between them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Accountability: research output converted into shipped product.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 3 External Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own customer, partner and vendor relationships directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Constructor Tech and Constructor University on joint offerings and teaching applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the group externally at conferences and with partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Success Metrics and KPIs: partner engagements initiated and sustained, external visibility of the group.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical background in physics, engineering or computer science, with enough depth to hold your own with research scientists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taken scientific or deep-tech software from research prototype to product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run customer and partner engagements personally, not through a sales team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Worked somewhere small enough that the product person also does the work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SLSQ427R368&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While candidates in the listed locations are encouraged for this role, we are open to remote candidates in other locations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This senior leadership role&lt;/strong&gt; will lead Partner Sales for the&amp;nbsp; Central EMEA region (Germany. CH, Austria eastern Europe), focused on consulting and Systems Integrator (C&amp;amp;SI) partners, as a member of the Regional Leadership Team. The regional leader will build the regional ecosystem strategy and plan aligned with regional and functional priorities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your direct reports will include Partner Sales managers/directors in the region. You will report to the Vice President, EMEA Alliances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Director, Partner Sales, you own the partner go-to-market strategy for the assigned region — driving co-sell motions in our top accounts, working with priority partners for co-sell and co-deliver, building durable pipelines, and holding partners accountable to execution that converts to partner-sourced and partner-influenced consumption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly visible, strategic role: you drive the partner-first motion across Sales, Field Engineering, Marketing, and work with the extended team of Partner Solution Architects, Partner Marketing, Partner Management and Partner Enablement. You carry Databricks&#39; regional partner narrative to senior partner executives in our partner ecosystem. You will own and grow executive relationships and commitment with strategic partners across the region — including global and regional systems integrators (e.g. Accenture, Deloitte, Capgemini) and specialist data and AI partners — and you bring deep industry knowledge and an operator&#39;s mindset powered by modern AI tooling.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2006&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The impact you will have: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Team Development&lt;/strong&gt; — Lead the regional Alliances/C&amp;amp;SI function, building and developing a high-performing cross-functional team while representing the partner organisation in regional leadership forums.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Planning &amp;amp; Ecosystem Leadership&lt;/strong&gt; — Own the multi-year regional partner territory plan — forming a compelling 3-year vision with partner segmentation, coverage model, and operational rhythm aligned to regional and functional priorities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Relationships &amp;amp; Narrative&lt;/strong&gt; — Own executive-level partner relationships, building joint business plans and executive-ready narratives that represent Databricks credibly to senior partner and customer leadership.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;

